<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Deliberately EMPTY. Every Hardened Runtime exception is attack surface.
       maknae needs none today.

       WATCH THIS SPACE - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation.
       Hardened Runtime enables library validation, which requires a loaded dylib
       to carry the SAME Team ID as the process. Maknae loads the AWS-LC FIPS
       module as a dylib on macOS (upstream requires shared linkage here), and
       AD-HOC signatures carry no Team ID at all - so an ad-hoc binary refuses an
       ad-hoc dylib with "different Team IDs" (measured 2026-09-12, rc 134).
       A real Developer ID signs both with ONE Team ID and is EXPECTED to satisfy
       library validation with no entitlement. That is NOT yet verified - verify it
       the day the certificate exists rather than assuming it. Until then, local
       dev builds may carry the entitlement on the DEV PATH ONLY; it must not reach
       a shipped artifact without its own recorded decision. -->
</dict>
</plist>
